# Advanced constructs, all in one file. Every item here must stay Opaque in
# this step; the file exists so the extent rules are exercised together.

separator:,
skip 1
fields date, description, amount, note

# A conditional TABLE. Its extent is terminated by the blank line below it, so
# that blank line travels with the table.
if,account2,comment
ACME PAYROLL,income:salary,monthly pay
%description COFFEE HOUSE,expenses:food:coffee,
LANDLORD LLC,expenses:home:rent,rent

# Stacked matchers, ANDed with && and negated with !. Tab-indented assignments.
if
%description SUPERMARKET
&& %note GROCERY
	account2  expenses:food:groceries
	comment1  weekly groceries

if
%description ONLINE
& ! %note REFUND
	account2  expenses:shopping

if ! %description TRANSFER
	account2  expenses:unknown

# A match group: capture the YYYY-MM prefix of the description and reuse it.
if %description (....-..)
	comment2  period \1

# A matcher that LOOKS like a comment. hledger reads this line as a regex, not
# as a comment, so the block matches any record containing a ';'. Ledgeline
# refuses to edit it rather than cement a reading the author probably did not
# intend — see OpaqueReason::CommentLikeMatcher.
if
; not actually a comment
	account2  expenses:unknown

if SKIP THIS ROW
	skip 1
	end
